  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e8ae2812-11f0-48c8-a39a-b3b30ed46927" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="64">
    <problem>
      <para>A Sierpinski triangle can be created by starting with an equilateral triangle, breaking the triangle into 4 congruent equilateral triangles, and then removing the middle triangle. Starting from a single black equilateral triangle with an area of 256 square inches, here are the first four steps:</para>
      <para><figure><media alt="A pattern of 4 congruent equilateral triangles. Starting with the first triangle, remove smaller congruent triangles to create the triangle to its right."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/846475c330baf5f005af08f87b151ae7cc7e047f"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Complete this table showing the number of shaded triangles in each step and the area of each triangle. Enter each answer as an integer.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-midsizetable">
        <thead>
          <row>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Step Number</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number Of Shaded Triangles</entry>
            <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Area Of One Shaded Triangle In Square Inches</entry>
          </row>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry>
              0
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              256
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              a.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              b.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              c.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              d.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              e.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              f.
            </entry>
            <entry>
              g.
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
      <para> In Step 1, what is the area of each shaded triangle in square inches? 
          </para>
        </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! 64; The area of each shaded triangle in square inches is 64.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.15.2.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--4b-->
